WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.760
Good morning, this is Environmental Intelligence Episode 47 for June 19, 2026.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:10.440
Your Environmental Intelligence briefing, wrapping up the week with the environmental

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:15.780
developments you need to know heading into the weekend. BC Minister of Environment and Parks

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:22.560
approves Red Chris Mindshift from Open Pit to Block Cave Mining via Environmental Assessment Certificate

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:29.020
Amendment. The sole provincial regulatory action today is the Red Chris Porphyry Copper Gold Mine

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:35.420
Amendment in British Columbia. A second BC item addresses fish habitat protection funding at

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:41.560
Ingle Lake. Practitioners working on mine permits or aquatic habitat projects in BC should

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:47.700
review both releases for compliance implications this week. If you only know one thing today for

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:53.180
your compliance calendar, British Columbia has approved an Environmental Assessment Certificate

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:59.720
Amendment for the Red Chris Mindblock Cave Transition. Mine operators and consultants handling

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:06.240
BC-EMA Environmental Assessment Certificates need to confirm whether current permits reference

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:12.360
open pit limits that now require updating. Tamara Davidson, Minister of Environment and Parks,

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:18.400
approved an amendment to the Red Chris Porphyry Copper Gold Mine Environmental Assessment Certificate,

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:23.020
authorizing the transition from Open Pit Mining to Underground Block Caving.

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:29.100
The change replaces surface extraction methods with underground techniques at the existing permitted

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:34.180
site. This alters the physical footprint and potential contaminant release pathways

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:40.360
compared with the original Open Pit design. Consultants managing similar Porphyry Copper Gold

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:46.900
projects under BC-EMA certificates should assess whether analogous amendments are feasible or

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:53.340
required for ongoing operations. No implementation timeline or additional monitoring conditions are

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:59.420
stated in the announcement. The Minister of Environment and Parks approved an amendment to the Red Chris

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:05.700
Porphyry Copper Gold Mine Environmental Assessment Certificate, authorizing the shift from Open Pit

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:11.300
to Block Cave Underground Mining. The change modifies the approved extraction method under the

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:17.960
existing certificate. Mine operators must verify that operational plans and monitoring programs align

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:24.480
with the amended certificate conditions. The BC Ministry of Water, Land, and Resource Stewardship

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:31.020
release details on provincial funding directed at Inga Lake. Funding supports fish habitat protection

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:36.880
at the site. Public access maintenance forms part of the supported activities. Conservation

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:42.880
infrastructure at Inga Lake receives attention through the allocation. The work addresses ongoing

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:49.540
habitat and access obligations under provincial water and land stewardship programs. Consultants

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:55.700
involved in fisheries habitat or access planning in northern BC should note the infrastructure focus.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:01.900
The announcement appears under the heading keeping Inga Lake accessible for public anglers.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:08.180
There's a nuance here worth understanding when a client submits a request to amend an existing EMA

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:14.980
certificate for a Porphyry deposit. Siting improved geotechnical stability and reduced surface

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:21.020
disturbance from shifting to Block Cave methods. The original certificate and supporting documents were

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:27.780
prepared under Open Pit Assumptions, so the hydrogeological model, seepage estimates, and waste rock

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:36.360
characterization no longer match the proposed extraction sequence. BCCRCR Protocol 1 requires that any

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:41.780
material change in mining method triggers re-evaluation of contaminant transport pathways,

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:48.460
and exposure scenarios before the amendment can be considered complete. Experienced assessors

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:54.160
recognize that Block Cave operations often create different fracture networks and dewatering

00:03:54.160 --> 00:04:00.200
demands than Open Pits, which can change ground water flow directions and metal leaching rates even

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:05.880
when total tonnage remains similar. The most common mistake is treating the amendment as a simple

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:11.160
footprint reduction and reusing the original risk assessment without updating the source term

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:18.400
and receptor pathway analysis. The fix is to rerun the fate and transport model with Block Cave specific

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:24.000
parameters before submitting the amendment package. If you're working on mine certificate amendments

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:30.540
in British Columbia, review the Red Chris Amendment Notice for language that may set precedent for

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:36.920
other BCC mine certificate changes. Confirm whether any current client projects reference Open Pit

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:44.220
limits that could now be revisited. Brief BCC mine clients on the need to update hydrogeological models

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:50.340
when extraction methods change. No specific upcoming federal or provincial consultation deadlines

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:57.320
were identified in today's sources. Monitor BCCgov news releases for further EMA certificate amendments

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:03.620
affecting mining operations. Tomorrow, watch for any follow-up announcements on additional BCC

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:10.080
mining certificate amendments. That covers today's environmental intelligence. If you found this useful,

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:14.600
share it with a colleague who needs to stay current. We'll be back with the next briefing.

